- # `↯/s.118.10` — `Tel.Provider.Error`
+ # `↯/s.118.10` — `Tel.Provider.Error`

- Raised when a TEL document does not conform to the schema a `Tel.Provider` reads it by.
+ Levée lorsqu'un document TEL n'est pas conforme au schéma selon lequel un `Tel.Provider` le lit.

- ## Cause
+ ## Cause

- Stratiform's `Tel.Provider` reads a document through its schema as a record's fields are read,
- and reports each mismatch through the `Tactic` of the code reading the field, so that a
- validating reader can collect them all. The message is `the TEL did not conform to its schema
- because $reason`.
+ Le `Tel.Provider` de Stratiform lit un document à travers son schéma à mesure que les champs
+ d'un enregistrement sont lus, et signale chaque discordance par la `Tactic` du code qui lit le
+ champ, afin qu'un lecteur validant puisse toutes les collecter. Le message est
+ `the TEL did not conform to its schema because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ### `↯/s.118.10.1` — `Absent`
+ ### `↯/s.118.10.1` — `Absent`

- A field the schema requires is missing from the document.
+ Un champ que le schéma exige est absent du document.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.118.10.1] the TEL did not conform to its schema because the field first-name is required`
+ **Exemple.** `[↯/s.118.10.1] the TEL did not conform to its schema because the field first-name is required`

- **Resolution.** Add the field, or make it optional in the schema.
+ **Résolution.** Ajoutez le champ, ou rendez-le optionnel dans le schéma.

- ### `↯/s.118.10.2` — `NotSigil`
+ ### `↯/s.118.10.2` — `NotSigil`

- A field read by the `Sigil` validator holds an atom of more than one character.
+ Un champ lu par le validateur `Sigil` contient un atome de plus d'un caractère.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.118.10.2] the TEL did not conform to its schema because the value ab is not a single character`
+ **Exemple.** `[↯/s.118.10.2] the TEL did not conform to its schema because the value ab is not a single character`

- **Resolution.** Give the field a single character.
+ **Résolution.** Donnez au champ un seul caractère.

